interface Clock is

   --  The system's time (ADR 0020). A reading is quantised to a tick,
   --  10 ms.

   function Monotonic return Word_64;
   --  Nanoseconds since the system was first started, not counting the
   --  time that it was off. Never goes backwards, including across a
   --  restore.

   function Realtime return Word_64;
   --  Nanoseconds since 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC, without leap seconds.
   --  It doesn't go backwards at a restore, and only Clock_Admin's
   --  Set_Realtime moves it backwards.

   function Realtime_Is_Trusted return Word;
   --  0 when Realtime is known to be a guess: the RTC's battery bit is
   --  clear, its fields are out of range, or the clock is held at the
   --  checkpoint's time after a restore. 1 otherwise, and again after
   --  Set_Realtime. (A function can't return a Boolean in IDL yet.)

end Clock;
